{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1551512350,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWU0MTYzNzA0Nzc=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3189","origin":"github"},"title":"Bring rev-create into -core","message":"Despite its core function, this is a leaf command from an implementation perspective. Introducing it into -core with first and foremost aid the import of -revolution tests that have been ported for better cross-platform performance.\n\nGiven there is already a `create` command, as deprecation cycle would be needed that could follow that of `rev-save` https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3188.\n\nKey difference of `create` and `rev-create` is a more compact API that focuses solely on the business of creating a dataset, and not on some aspects of its configuration.\n\nI suspect that the old `create` could be RF'ed to use `rev-save` and kept around for as long as deemed necessary to avoid needless disturbance of the API. `rev-create` is faster, though...","files":null}]}